{"parentUuid":"a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/synthetic/projects/parse-config","sessionId":"synthetic-quiz-fixture-001","version":"2.0.32","gitBranch":"fix/duration-units","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_synth_0007","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found it. Two defects in src/duration.ts: the \"s\" suffix is missing from UNIT_FACTORS entirely, and unknown suffixes silently fall through to a factor of 1 (milliseconds) via the `?? 1` default. So \"30s\" parses the digits, misses the unit, and returns 30 ms."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn"},"uuid":"a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007","timestamp":"2026-06-10T18:03:05.000Z"}
